:: Deadwood Street Mickey Offer
<<deadwood-street-story-header 'mickey' 0 'smuggler'>>
<<if !_storyPageUnavailable>>
  <<deadwood-dynamicblock 'deadwood-street-mickey-offer'>>
    <<set _mickeyStory to maplebirch.get('StreetLife').stories.state.mickey>>
    <<if _mickeyStory.stage is 0>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          Landry leaves a folded note beside your drink. There is no name on it, just an account of an argument outside the Ocean Breeze café and the date it was supposed to have happened. Underneath, someone has added that the police have been asking questions about paid jobs in town.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          兰德里把一张折过的便笺留在你的杯子旁。上面没有署名，只记着海风咖啡馆门前的一场争执，以及据说发生的日期。底下又添了一句，说警察正在打听镇上那些拿钱办事的人。
      <</language>><br><br>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          "It came back to me twice," <<nnpc_he 'Landry'>> says. "That doesn't mean two people saw it. Find out where it started before anyone puts money on it. Ask at the café first."
        <<option 'CN'>>
          “这消息传到我耳朵里两回了。”<<nnpc_he 'Landry'>>说，“可不一定是两个人亲眼见过。先查清是从哪儿传出来的，省得有人拿它当真。先去咖啡馆问问。”
      <</language>><br><br>
      <<if maplebirch.get('StreetLife').heist.mickeyAvailable>>
        <<language>>
          <<option 'EN'>>
            The narrow door beyond the partition is shut. You can hear a keyboard on the other side. Landry lowers <<nnpc_his 'Landry'>> voice. "Mickey can help untangle who told whom. You'll still have to check the story yourself."
          <<option 'CN'>>
            隔板后的窄门关着，门内传来敲键盘的声音。兰德里压低了声音。“米奇能帮你理清是谁传给谁的。消息是真是假，还得你自己去问。”
        <</language>><br><br>
        <<deadwood-street-story-choice 'mickey' 'assisted'>>
      <</if>>
      <<deadwood-street-story-choice 'mickey' 'self'>>
    <<else>>
      <<if _mickeyStory.source is 'assisted'>>
        <<language>>
          <<option 'EN'>>
            Mickey kept the door on its chain while they looked over the note. Their first question was whether either person claimed to have been there. After a few keystrokes, they pointed out that both accounts came from the same source. They suggested starting at the café, without telling the next person what answer you hoped to hear.
          <<option 'CN'>>
            核对便笺时，米奇始终没松开门链。对方先问两人是否声称自己在场，敲了几下键盘后，指出两条消息最早出自同一个人。接下来该去咖啡馆查证，不过问话时，别一开口就把想听的答案告诉人家。
        <</language>><br><br>
      <<elseif _mickeyStory.source is 'self'>>
        <<language>>
          <<option 'EN'>>
            You put the accounts side by side. The same odd phrase appears in both, although neither names a witness. Landry taps the date on the note. "Keep what they saw separate from what they heard. Bring me both."
          <<option 'CN'>>
            你把两人的说法并排记下。里面有一句用词出奇地相似，却都没提到谁亲眼见过。兰德里点了点便笺上的日期。“亲眼看见的，和听别人说的，分开记。都带回来。”
        <</language>><br><br>
      <</if>>
      <<deadwood-street-story-result 'mickey'>>
    <</if>>
  <</deadwood-dynamicblock>>
<</if>>
<<deadwood-street-story-leave 'smuggler'>>

:: Deadwood Street Mickey Cafe
<<deadwood-street-story-header 'mickey' 1 'cafe'>>
<<if !_storyPageUnavailable>>
  <<deadwood-dynamicblock 'deadwood-street-mickey-cafe'>>
    <<set _mickeyStory to maplebirch.get('StreetLife').stories.state.mickey>>
    <<if _mickeyStory.stage is 1>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          Cups clatter behind the counter. The server recognises the argument when you mention the café door, but pauses at the date on your note. "There was a delivery. Someone had the wrong address. I've heard a few versions since."
        <<option 'CN'>>
          柜台后传来杯盘相碰的声音。你提到门前的争执，店员倒是记得，却在看到便笺上的日期时停了一下。“是来送东西的，地址写错了。后来传成什么样的都有。”
      <</language>><br><br>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          A few receipts lie beneath a saucer by the till. The server can spare you a little time between orders. You could ask where each part of the story came from, or use the dates to establish what happened first.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          收银台旁的茶碟下压着几张单据。店员能趁接单的空隙陪你核对一会儿。你可以问清每种说法是从谁那里听来的，也可以先对一对日期，看看事情的先后。
      <</language>><br><br>
      <<deadwood-street-story-choice 'mickey' 'listen'>>
      <<deadwood-street-story-choice 'mickey' 'observe'>>
    <<else>>
      <<if _mickeyStory.stage gt 2>>
        <<language>>
          <<option 'EN'>>
            The server has gone back to taking orders. You have written down where the café's account came from; there is nothing more to ask here.
          <<option 'CN'>>
            店员已经回去接单了。咖啡馆里这些说法的来源，你都记在了纸上，这里没有别的线索可问了。
        <</language>><br><br>
      <<elseif _mickeyStory.result is 'success'>>
        <<language>>
          <<option 'EN'>>
            The argument happened, but earlier than the note claims. Nobody here saw the police question either person involved. That part was brought in afterwards by a customer who had been working near the industrial alleyways. You have a place to check next, and a clearer idea of what still needs checking.
          <<option 'CN'>>
            争执确有其事，却比便笺上写的早。这里没人亲眼见过警察盘问争执的双方。那部分是后来一位在工业巷道附近做事的客人说的。你知道下一步该去哪里，也分清了还有哪句话没得到证实。
        <</language>><br><br>
      <<else>>
        <<language>>
          <<option 'EN'>>
            The argument was real. Beyond that, the dates and second-hand accounts refuse to line up. The server remembers that the talk about police questions came from a customer working near the industrial alleyways. It is something to follow, though you still cannot tell how much the customer saw.
          <<option 'CN'>>
            争执确实发生过，可日期和转述的说法始终对不上。店员只记得，警察打听消息的说法来自一位在工业巷道附近做事的客人。这条线还能接着查，只是暂时弄不清对方究竟见过多少。
        <</language>><br><br>
      <</if>>
      <<deadwood-street-story-result 'mickey'>>
    <</if>>
  <</deadwood-dynamicblock>>
<</if>>
<<deadwood-street-story-leave 'cafe'>>

:: Deadwood Street Mickey Alley
<<deadwood-street-story-header 'mickey' 2 'alley'>>
<<if !_storyPageUnavailable>>
  <<deadwood-dynamicblock 'deadwood-street-mickey-alley'>>
    <<set _mickeyStory to maplebirch.get('StreetLife').stories.state.mickey>>
    <<if _mickeyStory.stage is 2>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          A trolley rattles over the paving behind a loading door. The café customer is easy enough to find. They remember the delivery and repeat much of what is on Landry's note, but the mention of police came from someone else.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          装卸门后，一辆手推车从砖地上颠过。咖啡馆的那位客人并不难找。对方记得送货的事，说法也与兰德里便笺上的大致相同，只是一提到警察，就说那是从别人那里听来的。
      <</language>><br><br>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          Another worker is waiting beside a stack of empty pallets. You have not spoken to them yet. They might remember the questions themselves, rather than another telling of the same story.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          另一名工人正等在一摞空托盘旁。你还没问过对方。比起再听一遍传闻，或许能从这里找到真正被问过话的人。
      <</language>><br><br>
      <<deadwood-street-story-choice 'mickey' 'second'>>
    <<else>>
      <<if _mickeyStory.choice is 'second' and _mickeyStory.outcome is 'verified'>>
        <<language>>
          <<option 'EN'>>
            With the separate accounts beside one another, the dates are clearer. The police questions concerned an older theft, before the argument at the café. You have kept your own associates' names out of it. Two separate incidents have been passed around as one warning.
          <<option 'CN'>>
            把各处听来的说法放到一起，日期便清楚了。警察问话涉及的是更早的一桩失窃案，发生在咖啡馆争执之前。你没有提起自己这边的人。两件不同的事，被传成了同一个警告。
        <</language>><br><br>
      <<elseif _mickeyStory.choice is 'second'>>
        <<language>>
          <<option 'EN'>>
            The worker remembers questions about a theft, but cannot place the day. You find nothing to tie that inquiry to the argument at the café. It is not enough to dismiss every warning, or to claim that anyone is being watched.
          <<option 'CN'>>
            工人记得有人来问过失窃的事，却说不准是哪一天。你没有找到证据，能把那次问话和咖啡馆的争执连在一起。还不能说风声全是假的，也不能断定有人正被盯着。
        <</language>><br><br>
      <</if>>
      <<deadwood-street-story-result 'mickey'>>
    <</if>>
  <</deadwood-dynamicblock>>
<</if>>
<<deadwood-street-story-leave 'alley'>>

:: Deadwood Street Mickey Police
<<deadwood-street-story-header 'mickey' 2 'police'>>
<<if !_storyPageUnavailable>>
  <<deadwood-dynamicblock 'deadwood-street-mickey-police'>>
    <<set _mickeyStory to maplebirch.get('StreetLife').stories.state.mickey>>
    <<if _mickeyStory.stage is 2>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          Grant listens to the date and place on the note. He rests a hand on the register beside him. "A story passed around a pub isn't a statement. What did anyone actually see?"
        <<option 'CN'>>
          格兰特听过便笺上的日期和地点，伸手按住身旁的登记簿。“酒馆里传的话算不上证词。究竟有谁亲眼见过？”
      <</language>><br><br>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You keep to the café argument and the earlier delivery. He is willing to check whether they concern an existing case. "I'll tell you what I can. That doesn't make me responsible for whatever you decide to do with it."
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你只问咖啡馆的争执，以及更早的那次送货。他愿意查查是否涉及已有的案子。“能说的，我会告诉你。别拿着我的话，说我替谁担了保。”
      <</language>><br><br>
      <<deadwood-street-story-choice 'mickey' 'police'>>
    <<else>>
      <<if _mickeyStory.choice is 'police' and _mickeyStory.outcome is 'police'>>
        <<language>>
          <<option 'EN'>>
            Grant can confirm an older theft inquiry, but the details you have brought do not identify everyone involved. He will not fill the gaps with guesses. "There may be further questions. That's all you should repeat."
          <<option 'CN'>>
            格兰特能确认之前有人调查过一桩失窃案，但你带来的细节还不足以确定涉及哪些人。他不肯拿猜测填补空缺。“之后还可能有人来问。你要转述，就只说这一句。”
        <</language>><br><br>
      <</if>>
      <<deadwood-street-story-result 'mickey'>>
    <</if>>
  <</deadwood-dynamicblock>>
<</if>>
<<deadwood-street-story-leave 'police'>>

:: Deadwood Street Mickey Debrief
<<deadwood-street-story-header 'mickey' 3 'smuggler'>>
<<if !_storyPageUnavailable>>
  <<deadwood-dynamicblock 'deadwood-street-mickey-debrief'>>
    <<set _mickeyStory to maplebirch.get('StreetLife').stories.state.mickey>>
    <<if _mickeyStory.stage is 3>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          Landry moves <<nnpc_his 'Landry'>> glass aside to make room for the note. The fold is wearing thin, and there are more dates on it now. "Which parts can I use?"
        <<option 'CN'>>
          兰德里把杯子挪开，让出一块放便笺的地方。纸上的折痕已有些发软，也多了几行日期。“哪几句能当真？”
      <</language>><br><br>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You separate the witnesses from the people repeating them, and leave the gaps in the account. Landry reads it through once without interrupting. "I'd rather know where it stops than pay for a better ending."
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你把亲眼见过的人与转述消息的人分开记下，没查清的地方就空着。兰德里从头看完，没有打断。“知道查到哪儿就够了。我可不花钱买个编出来的结尾。”
      <</language>><br><br>
      <<deadwood-street-story-choice 'mickey' 'settle'>>
    <<else>>
      <<if _mickeyStory.outcome is 'verified'>>
        <<language>>
          <<option 'EN'>>
            Landry draws a line beneath the confirmed dates. "Good. I can work with that." The old warning will not be treated as fresh news, and the unconfirmed names stay off <<nnpc_his 'Landry'>> list. <<nnpc_He 'Landry'>> folds the note away and counts out your payment.
          <<option 'CN'>>
            兰德里在已经核实的日期下划了道线。“行，这个能用。”旧风声不会再当成新消息，未经证实的名字也没被记上<<nnpc_his 'Landry'>>的名单。<<nnpc_He 'Landry'>>收好便笺，数出你的报酬。
        <</language>><br><br>
      <<elseif _mickeyStory.outcome is 'police'>>
        <<language>>
          <<option 'EN'>>
            Landry pauses when you mention Grant. "What he told you, then. Leave out what you think he meant." <<nnpc_He 'Landry'>> keeps the warning about further inquiries beside the dates you checked. Your visit concerned an old case; you have promised the detective nothing about another job.
          <<option 'CN'>>
            听见格兰特的名字，兰德里停了一下。“他说过什么，就记什么。别把你猜他是什么意思也算进去。”<<nnpc_He 'Landry'>>把还会有人走访的提醒留在核对过的日期旁。你这一趟问的是旧案，并没向警探许诺另一桩差事。
        <</language>><br><br>
      <<else>>
        <<language>>
          <<option 'EN'>>
            Landry reads the gaps as carefully as the rest. "At least you haven't sold me a guess." <<nnpc_He 'Landry'>> sets aside a smaller payment. The story has not been settled, so anyone acting on it will still have to allow for that uncertainty.
          <<option 'CN'>>
            兰德里把那些空白处也看了一遍。“起码你没拿猜的来糊弄我。”<<nnpc_He 'Landry'>>拨出一份少些的报酬。风声还没完全查清，往后真要据此做事，也得给这些没底的地方留点余地。
        <</language>><br><br>
      <</if>>
      <<deadwood-street-story-result 'mickey'>>
    <</if>>
  <</deadwood-dynamicblock>>
<</if>>
<<deadwood-street-story-leave 'smuggler'>>
